---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---

<Layout
	title="Support & Contact"
	description="Troubleshooting, purchase support, feedback, and contact information for VideoVault."
	canonicalPath="/support/"
>
	<article class="legal container">
		<nav class="legal__nav" aria-label="Legal">
			<a href="/">Home</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.privacy}>Privacy Policy</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.terms}>Terms of Use</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.support} aria-current="page">Support</a>
		</nav>

		<h1>VideoVault Support &amp; Contact</h1>
		<p class="legal__meta">Help with VideoVault: Media Player for iPhone and iPad.</p>

		<a class="button" href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}?subject=VideoVault%20Feedback`}>
			Send Feedback
		</a>
		<p>
			Email:{' '}
			<a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}?subject=VideoVault%20Support`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>
		</p>
		<p>We aim to respond to valid support requests within three business days.</p>

		<h2>What we can help with</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Lifetime Pro purchase, entitlement, and Restore Purchase issues</li>
			<li>Media import, playback, Picture in Picture, and background playback</li>
			<li>Audio extraction, background music, volume adjustment, recording, export, and sharing</li>
			<li>Full Library Backup and Restore</li>
			<li>Bug reports, accessibility issues, and feature suggestions</li>
			<li>Privacy questions</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Information to include</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>VideoVault version and build number</li>
			<li>Device model and iOS/iPadOS version</li>
			<li>A short description of what happened</li>
			<li>Steps that reliably reproduce the issue</li>
			<li>The result you expected</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Do not send private media, passwords, Apple Account credentials, payment card information, or
			sensitive personal information.
		</p>

		<h2>Backup and data recovery</h2>
		<p>
			Deleting VideoVault can remove locally stored media and playlists. Before deleting the app or
			changing devices, use <strong>Settings → Data &amp; Backup → Export Full Backup</strong> and
			save the file to iCloud Drive or another external location.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Restore Purchase</strong> restores Lifetime Pro access. It does not restore media. Use
			<strong> Restore from Backup</strong> to restore media and playlists from a VideoVault backup
			file.
		</p>

		<h2>Purchase and refund questions</h2>
		<p>
			Lifetime Pro is a non-consumable purchase processed by Apple. For billing or refund requests, use
			Apple’s purchase support channels. For an entitlement that should be active but is not, first
			use <strong>Restore Purchase</strong>, then contact us if the issue continues.
		</p>

		<h2>Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			Support email is user-initiated. We use information you send only to respond, investigate the
			issue, improve VideoVault, and maintain reasonable support records. See the{' '}
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.privacy}>Privacy Policy</a>.
		</p>
	</article>
</Layout>
